  "report": {
   "iso_week": "2026-W41",
   "engine": "template",
   "narrative": "This report describes published K-Electric load-shed schedules effective from 2026-08-05; they are schedules, not measured outages. K-Electric lists 623 feeders under load shed across 30 IBC areas, of which 617 have a schedule row. Among listed feeders with a schedule, 492 are scheduled for twelve hours a day and 125 for six (79.7% at twelve hours); exempt feeders are not published, so these shares cover listed feeders only.\n\nAmong IBC areas with at least ten scheduled feeders, the highest share at twelve hours is in IBC - Clifton (100%, n = 11) and the lowest in IBC - Johar - I (46.7%, n = 15). 2 IBC areas have every scheduled listed feeder at twelve hours.\n\nScheduled hours correspond to the published loss category; 2 Medium-category feeders are the exceptions at twelve hours. Category is not a pure function of the published loss figure: in the loss band where the Medium and High categories overlap there are 112 Medium and 89 High feeders. This is an observation about the published categories, not a finding about fairness.\n\nExploratory rank correlations (descriptive only; no significance or causal reading): across listed feeders, loss and scheduled hours have Spearman rho = 0.676 (n = 615). At census sub-division level, using the 15 IBC areas matched by name to 13 sub-divisions, the share of listed feeders at twelve hours has rho = -0.39 with literacy and rho = -0.258 with the degree-holder share (n = 13).",
